# E08 Contract Net Protocol: parallel; the three postmen print their status and the protocol in any order between them
# (a status block is written at once, but which postman comes first depends on the interleaving). Compared as
# multisets: the status lines (names, tours solved by the TSP of the example, payoffs), the messages of the protocol,
# and what each postman does with them. One CNPMessage object is shared by every receiver of a broadcast and changed
# in place by each (X13): the values a receiver prints depend on who handled the object first, in the C# as in the
# C++, so the messages are compared without them; the values are compared where the agent that computes them prints
# them.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact name ^(postman\d)$
fact tour ^Tour: (.*)$
fact payoff ^Payoff: (.*)$
fact message ^(postman\d) -> (postman\d): (\w+) (L\d\d) -?\d+\.\d\d -?\d+\.\d\d -?\d+\.\d\d$
fact cfp ^(postman\d) receives cfp (L\d\d) with (.*)$
fact proposal ^(postman\d) receives proposal (L\d\d) with (.*)$
fact given ^(postman\d) is given (L\d\d) with (.*)$
same name bag
same tour bag
same payoff bag
same message bag
same cfp bag
same proposal bag
same given bag
check name count == 6
check name distinct(0) == 3
